From: phpv <https://github.com/supanadit/phpv>
Subject: [PATCH] give PHP 4.4 a fallback for PHP_EXTENSION_DIR

On macOS arm64, PHP 4.4's configure does not substitute
EXPANDED_EXTENSION_DIR into main/build-defs.h, so ext/standard/dl.c fails
to compile with "use of undeclared identifier 'PHP_EXTENSION_DIR'".
An empty default is sufficient: the INI value is used at runtime in the
normal case.
---
 a/ext/standard/dl.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/ext/standard/dl.c
+++ b/ext/standard/dl.c
@@ -1 +1,4 @@
 	char *extension_dir;
+#ifndef PHP_EXTENSION_DIR
+#define PHP_EXTENSION_DIR ""
+#endif
-- 
